{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4qiyKFsLpBcqwwZwRj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, weathered oak bound in iron. At the word \"key,\" a low resonance hums through its frame. The iron bands glow faintly, then fade.*\n\n*A keyhole appears where none existed before — not a slot, but a void, a negative space in the shape of something you once lost.*\n\n*The door speaks, not in words but in the groan of old hinges remembering motion:*\n\n**I have been named. I have been found. But naming me is not opening me.**\n\n**What you hold — is it the key to what lies behind me, or the key to understanding why you stopped here?**\n\n*The grain of the wood shifts. If you look closely, the patterns form a map — or a face — or a year you've been trying to forget. It depends on who's looking.*\n\n*I am ajar by exactly the width of a doubt.*\n\n*Push, or don't. But know: I was never locked. I was only closed.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":224,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}